# Demo Bot Engine — AI-Automated Side Hustle

## Background

Cold outreach on marketplaces like Upwork is saturated: by the time a request is found, 10+ freelancers have already pitched. The insight behind this project is to flip the dynamic — instead of *telling* a prospect what AI can do for them, *show* them with a working demo built from their own public website, delivered as a single link. Nothing is needed from the prospect to receive it. If they want it live on their site, they pay. If not, the demo auto-deletes and we move on.

The whole loop — lead sourcing, demo generation, outreach, follow-ups — is designed to be automated, with humans only handling replies from interested prospects.

## Intent

Build a mostly-automated micro-agency selling custom AI chatbots to local service businesses (HVAC, dental, law, contractors, etc.):

1. **Scrape** a prospect's website for brand voice, services, and FAQs.
2. **Generate** a working demo chatbot grounded in that content (no hallucinations about prices/hours).
3. **Deliver** a personalized demo link via automated cold email.
4. **Convert** interested replies into the $500 Chat Doorman Setup + $200/mth Care Plan (hosting + updates).
5. **Expire** unclaimed demos automatically after 14 days to control hosting costs.

Target economics: 200 outreach emails/week → ~3–5% reply rate → a handful of sales calls → 1–3 clients/month. One client covers the entire infrastructure many times over.

## How it works

```
Prospect URL
    │
    ▼
scraper.py ── pulls homepage + /about, /services, /faq, /contact
    │          (capped text so prompts stay cheap; ~15KB max)
    │          (SSRF guard: refuses private/link-local targets)
    ▼
profile ── {brand, domain, corpus, faqs_detected}
    │
    ▼
bot.py ── builds a system prompt from the corpus, calls OpenRouter.
    │      Guardrails: answers ONLY from site content, says
    │      "I don't know" otherwise, never invents prices/hours/services.
    ▼
store.py ── SQLite persistence (survives restarts; TTL + /cleanup)
    │
    ▼
server.py ── FastAPI app hosting each demo at a personalized
             slug: /demo/acmeplumbing-a1b2c3
             + tracking links (/go, /pixel), embed snippet, /pay
```

