### Endpoints

| Route | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `GET /health` | Liveness + demo counts |
| `GET /models` | Model catalog + default |
| `POST /create` | `{url, model?}` → demo/go/pixel/embed URLs (**admin**) |
| `POST /request` | `{site_url, email}` → demo URLs + link emailed (public; rate-limited + creation-capped) |
| `GET /demo/{slug}` | Chat UI (`?embed=1` for compact widget mode) |
| `POST /api/chat/{slug}` | Chat API (multi-turn) |
| `GET /go/{slug}` | Tracked click → redirects to the demo |
| `GET /pixel/{slug}.gif` | 1×1 open-tracking pixel |
| `GET /pay/{slug}` | Tracked click → Stripe payment link |
| `GET /embed/{slug}` | Copy-paste "go live" snippet page |
| `GET /embed/{slug}.js` | Floating white-label widget |
| `GET /stats/{slug}` | Opens/clicks/chats/paid_clicks (**admin**) |
| `POST /keepalive/{slug}` | `{days}` → extend/renew a demo (YES flow) (**admin**) |
| `POST /cleanup` | Purge expired demos (**admin**) |

Admin routes require an `X-Admin-Token` header matching `ADMIN_TOKEN` (fail closed if unset).

`POST /request` is the public self-serve funnel and is rate-limited to
`REQUESTS_PER_HOUR` requests (default 5) per client key: `remote_addr` by
default, or — only when `TRUSTED_PROXIES` (int ≥ 1) is set — the entry
appended by the Nth trusted hop counting from the right of `X-Forwarded-For`
(XFF[-N]); the attacker-controlled leftmost entries are never used, and a
short XFF chain fails closed to `remote_addr`. A spoof-resilient global cap
`MAX_DEMOS_PER_HOUR` (default 30) bounds demo creations per hour across all
clients. Request bodies over 16KB are refused with 413 before parsing.
Caveats: the counters are in-memory — they reset on restart and are per
container instance. Missing SMTP, verified-TLS or CAN-SPAM config never blocks
the funnel: the demo is created regardless and the response carries
`emailed: false`. Email links are built only from `PUBLIC_BASE_URL` (unset →
the send is skipped). Error bodies use the engine's `{"detail": ...}` string
shape; FastAPI body-validation failures (422) use the default detail **list**
shape (`{"detail": [{...}]}`) instead.

### Model catalog

| OpenRouter id | Label | Type | Role |
|---|---|---|---|
| `openai/gpt-4.1-nano` | GPT-4.1 Nano | non-reasoning | **Default** — fastest/cheapest verified (~$0.00002/msg) |
| `openai/gpt-6-luna` | GPT-6 Luna | reasoning | Upgrade — cheap, self-skips thinking on easy prompts |
| `xiaomi/mimo-v2.6-pro` | MiMo-V2.6-Pro | reasoning | Upgrade — warmest follow-ups on the "don't know" path |
| `meta/muse-spark-1.3` | Muse Spark 1.3 | reasoning | Upgrade — warmest tone, ~5x slower and ~150x costlier/msg |

Verified against OpenRouter live: all four hold the grounding line (refuse to
invent prices) thanks to the system prompt — chain-of-thought isn't what
enforces it. Non-reasoning models answer in ~1.5s vs 5–9s for the reasoning
ones on this workload.

Set the default with `OPENROUTER_MODEL`, or pin one per demo: `POST /create {"url": ..., "model": "meta/muse-spark-1.3"}`. Unknown models are rejected.

