## ChatDoorman launch checklist

ChatDoorman.com is the product domain. Two DNS plays:

**1. Sending domain — warm it starting today (14 calendar days, no shortcut).**
Cold volume on a virgin domain lands in spam; warmup builds sender reputation
by having your mailbox trade real conversations with the ESP's warmup pool.

- Buy a **secondary** for cold (~$12/yr): `trychatdoorman.com`, `getchatdoorman.com`
  or `chatdoormanmail.com` — keep `chatdoorman.com` itself for product mail.
- DNS at the registrar: SPF + DKIM + DMARC (`p=none` now, `quarantine` later)
  using the exact records Instantly/Smartlead show you. Also their tracking CNAME.
- Create 1–2 mailboxes on the sending domain, add them to Instantly/Smartlead,
  enable **warmup**, leave it for 14 days. Volume ramp after: 25/day/inbox,
  never 50+ in month 1.
- During warmup: run `pipeline.py --max 10`, load the sequence copy, have the
  Stripe link ready. Day 15 → launch.

**2. Demo links on `demo.chatdoorman.com`.** `azurecontainerapps.io` URLs look
cold in a first-touch email. Create a CNAME `demo.chatdoorman.com` → the app
FQDN, then deploy with `-DemoHostname demo.chatdoorman.com` (creates a managed
cert + binds it), and set `PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://demo.chatdoorman.com`.
`UNSUBSCRIBE_URL` can be `https://chatdoorman.com/unsubscribe` (or the ESP's
built-in link — Instantly/Smartlead manage suppression for you).

Sender identity in the templates is `SENDER_NAME` (default "Clint") — set it to
whatever matches the mailbox you send from.

## Deployment on Azure

You're already on Azure, so stay there — it's **not** way more expensive. Two good options:

### Option A: Azure Container Apps (recommended — cheapest)

Consumption plan with scale-to-zero. Demos get sporadic traffic, so you mostly pay nothing:

- **Pricing (verified Sept 2026):** $0.000024/vCPU-sec active, $0.000003 idle, $0.40/million requests.
- **Free grant per subscription/month:** 180,000 vCPU-seconds + 360,000 GiB-seconds + 2M requests — worth ~100–200 active replica-hours at the smallest size (0.25 vCPU / 0.5 GiB).
- **Realistic cost for this workload:** **~$1–$15/month**, possibly $0 in quiet months. One analysis of a similar single-tenant app showed ~$14.60/mo with scale-to-zero vs ~$24.80 always-on.
- Cold starts are ~1–3s on consumption — fine for demo links in emails.

Ready-made script (review before running — it creates billable resources):

```powershell
$env:OPENROUTER_API_KEY = "sk-or-..."
./deploy/deploy.ps1 -ResourceGroup demo-bot-rg -AcrName demobotreg `
  -AppName demo-bot -EnvName demo-env -Location eastus
```

It does: `az group create` → `az acr create` → `az acr build` → `az containerapp env create` →
`az containerapp create` (min 0 / max 3 replicas, secrets via `secretref`), prints the FQDN,
and reminds you to set `PUBLIC_BASE_URL`. The raw commands are in `deploy/deploy.ps1`.

### Option B: Azure App Service B1 (simplest)

- **Pricing (verified Sept 2026):** Linux B1 = **$13.14/month** flat, always-on, custom domain + free TLS included.
- Predictable bill, zero cold starts, dead-simple deploys from GitHub Actions.
- Pick this if you'd rather pay a fixed $13 than think about consumption meters.

### Verdict

| | Hetzner VPS | Container Apps | App Service B1 |
|---|---|---|---|
| Cost | ~$5/mo | ~$1–15/mo | $13.14/mo |
| Ops | You manage the VM | Fully managed | Fully managed |
| Cold starts | No | ~1–3s | No |

Since you're already paying ~$107/mo on Azure, adding $1–13 for this is noise — and it keeps billing, identity, and monitoring in one place. **Go with Container Apps** unless you hate cold starts, then B1.

> Storage note: demos live in SQLite at `/app/data/demos.db`. `deploy/deploy.ps1`
> creates an Azure Storage account + file share and mounts it at `/app/data`, so
> demos survive restarts and scale-to-zero — emailed links stay live for the full
> TTL. `entrypoint.sh` fixes mount ownership and drops to an unprivileged user
> when the share allows it (loud warning if not). Swap the store for Azure Table
> Storage later only if multi-replica writes ever matter.

## Outreach (automated)

Full playbook in `docs/blueprint.md`. One command does sourcing → filtering →
email finding/verification → demo generation → outreach CSV:

```powershell
python src/pipeline.py --niche "aesthetic med spa" --location "Atlanta GA" --max 200
```

Needs `OUTSCRAPER_API_KEY`, `HUNTER_API_KEY`, `ADMIN_TOKEN`, `DEMO_SERVER_URL`.
Start with `--max 10` to check credit burn (Outscraper bills per result; Hunter
bills per domain-search + verify). The CSV it writes feeds the next two steps
directly (`business_name`, `first_name`, `email`, `go_url`, `pixel_url`,
`expires_at`).

Decomposed equivalent (also the path for pre-downloaded exports):

```powershell
# 1. raw Google Maps export (Outscraper/Apify) -> filtered, verified leads
python src/leads.py --in examples/raw-leads.csv --out data/leads.csv --verify --find-emails
#    drops: no website, already has a chat widget, chains (10+ locations),
#    opted-out contacts; Hunter domain-search + verification (info@ fallback)

# 2. leads -> per-lead demo links (skip if pipeline.py already made them)
python src/batch.py --in data/leads.csv --out data/demos.csv --server https://<host> --token $ADMIN_TOKEN

# 3. demos -> rendered 3-touch sequence (fail-closed without CAN-SPAM config)
$env:POSTAL_ADDRESS = "1 Main St, Austin TX 78701"
$env:UNSUBSCRIBE_URL = "https://chatdoorman.com/unsubscribe"
python src/outreach.py --in data/demos.csv --out data/emails.csv
python src/outreach.py --copy   # paste this into the Instantly/Smartlead editor

# 4. emails -> ESP campaign (dry run first; writes payloads.json for review)
python src/campaign.py --in data/emails.csv --provider instantly --campaign <id>
python src/campaign.py --in data/emails.csv --provider instantly --campaign <id> --send
```

Send discipline: separate sending domain warmed 14 days, 25–50 emails/day/inbox,
auto-stop on reply (ESP setting). The open pixel and tracked `go_url` CTA are
baked into every touch. When a prospect replies YES:

```powershell
python src/closer.py --slug acmeplumbing-a1b2c3 --token $ADMIN_TOKEN `
  --first-name Jane --business-name "Acme Plumbing" --out data/replies/acmeplumbing.txt
# keeps the demo alive + renders the go-live reply (embed snippet + Stripe link)
```

Convert: you handle replies (~15 min/day). Kill niches under 3% reply rate after
200 sends; double down over 5%. Watch `paid_clicks` in `/stats/{slug}`.

Email 1 template (rendered by `outreach.py`, footer + pixel appended automatically):

> Subject: quick demo for {BusinessName}
>
> Hey {FirstName} — we built a quick AI assistant demo for {BusinessName} from your website. It answers FAQs and captures after-hours leads.
>
> Try it here (60 sec, nothing to install): {go_url}
>
> Nothing needed from you — if you like it, reply and we'll put it live on your site. If not, it auto-deletes in 14 days.
>
> — Clint

