## Decisions log

- 2026-10-02 (R2 micro-round, R13 review): extraction correctness — accented/non-ASCII names capture in full (`my name is José García` → `José García`) and a name word cut mid-word is rejected, never partially stored; the date guard only rejects genuine Y-M-D/D-M-Y date shapes, so `+1 202 555 2020`, `+1 (415) 555-1985`, `1-800-555-1999` and `+44 20 7946 2000` all capture as phones; a contact cut by the 2000-char scan window is discarded instead of stored truncated; name intros are exactly the spec's four patterns (`my name is`/`name's`/`this is`/`it's` — bare `its` dropped) and weekday names are stopwords (month names are not: `my name is May` → `May`).
- 2026-10-02 (R1 hardening, R12 review): lead extraction is now bounded and adversarial-input-safe — each user message is scanned only up to its first 2000 chars with linear, non-overlapping patterns (a single 40KB hostile POST could previously stall the whole server ~18s), phone capture accepts only ASCII `[0-9]` 10–12-digit runs (cards, all 13+ digit runs and genuine date shapes are rejected; a bare 10–12-digit order ID can still be captured as a phone — the length gate is the rule), name capture requires an explicit intro (`my name is`/`name's`/`this is`/`it's`) with 1–2 initial-capital non-stopword words (`X here` dropped), dedupe hits backfill empty name/email/phone fields (two-step capture completes one lead), leads cap at 200 per demo (oldest dropped) and `/stats` emits at most that, and the sanitizer collapses whitespace runs to single spaces and strips Unicode Cc/Zl/Zp + bidi-format chars before storage and `/stats` emission.
- 2026-10-02: The chat now actually captures after-hours leads — `POST /api/chat/{slug}` extracts name + phone/email volunteered in user messages (control chars stripped, lengths capped at the boundary) and stores them on the demo row, deduped on email or phone (repeats update `last_seen`); admin `GET /stats/{slug}` returns them under `leads`, and chat responses never echo lead data. The prompt asks for name + best phone or email in the same reply as any follow-up offer and confirms the capture restating what the visitor gave — the API records unconditionally of the model's wording.
